  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Auto volumes stay soft and the China JV customer mix keeps shrinking in FY27, but domestic-OEM, India and thermal-management wins plus IPG's liquid-cooling pumps restore ~2.5-3% growth; adjusted EBITDA margin back to a mid-cycle 15%, capex normalising after the India expansion. Net cash of ~US$0.58bn is a fifth of the market cap.",
    "bull": "The new-growth optionality the market priced in 2025 (AI liquid cooling, humanoid-robot actuators, SOFC components) starts to show in sales, and APG's re-positioning toward domestic Chinese OEMs works; growth runs 5-6% mid-decade and margins return to the FY18-19 peak of ~16.5%.",
    "bear": "The China JV share loss and US tariff regime compound a light-vehicle downturn: two years of falling sales, margins stuck at the FY22-23 trough, copper costs not fully recovered, and the robotics/cooling bets remain rounding errors."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Mid-cycle owner-FCF valuation of a net-cash global auto/industrial motor supplier. The 2025 AI/robotics re-rating has fully unwound; the question now is whether a business earning ~US$175m owner FCF with ~US$0.58bn net cash is worth more than its ~US$2.0bn market cap on ordinary auto-supplier economics, with the new businesses treated as bull-case optionality only.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Light-vehicle production cycle and APG's 84% revenue weight",
      "Pace of Sino-foreign JV share loss in China versus domestic-OEM wins",
      "US tariff regime and in-region-for-region relocation costs",
      "Copper and input-cost pass-through lag compressing margins",
      "Capex staying at the FY26 7.9% level rather than normalising",
      "Impairment / M&A integration risk (US$22.4m European intangible impairment FY26)"
    ]
